  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-1",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -232,
      "w": 430,
      "text": "Circle, people-first.\nThe row carries all four things at once: today's status, progress, an opted-in reflection, and the latest achievement. Groups are the filter chips and the section beneath \u2014 never the primary object."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-2",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 940,
      "y": -232,
      "w": 430,
      "text": "This is the screen the new user failed on.\nCreate, browse and a code field are all on it, labelled. Nothing hides behind a \"Manage\" link or a bottom sheet."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-3",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 2350,
      "y": -232,
      "w": 430,
      "text": "Solo-or-shared is a FIELD here, not a modal fork.\nThis is what replaces showNewPlanPicker \u2014 one flow, asked in context, after you already know what you're reading."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-4",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": -232,
      "w": 430,
      "text": "Path owns the plan lifecycle.\nSolo and shared plans in one list, with Adjust pace on the card \u2014 the answer to \"where do I edit my plan\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-5",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -186,
      "w": 430,
      "text": "B is the pick \u2014 icons alone at rest, the active tab the only one labelled.\nEvery screen on page 1 uses it. A, C and D are kept for the record."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-6",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 470,
      "y": -232,
      "w": 430,
      "text": "Every status a row can carry.\nAde tapped the bare \"I read today\" button and has no plan at all. Sam has a plan, showed up, and still has Genesis 12 to read \u2014 both true at once. The habit never advances a plan, so a habit-only row must never show a reading reference.\n\nAchievements are not plan-tied either: Ade's 30 days is pure consistency."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
